              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you run a fleet or operate your own truck, you already know how important every moving part on your trailer is. When something goes wrong with a lift axle, it can quickly lead to uneven tire wear, handling issues, downtime, or even failed inspections. For owner-operators and fleet managers alike, understanding the basics of lift axle troubleshooting can save time, money, and frustration.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we know that when your equipment is down, your business slows down with it. That's why our team works hard to provide dependable trailer service, quality semi trailer parts, and straightforward support that helps keep you on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-warning-signs",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Signs You May Need Lift Axle Troubleshooting",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "warning-signs"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Lift axles are designed to improve weight distribution and reduce wear on your trailer. But like any mechanical system, they require regular inspection and maintenance. Catching problems early can help prevent more expensive repairs later.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Here are some common warning signs to watch for:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-warning-signs-3",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "bullet",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Lift axle not raising or lowering properly"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Uneven tire wear"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Air leaks near suspension components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Poor weight distribution"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Trailer leaning to one side"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Excessive vibration while driving"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension warning lights or system alerts"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-warning-signs-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Ignoring these issues can lead to bigger suspension or axle problems over time. Proper trailer preventive maintenance checklist routines can help reduce unexpected breakdowns and improve safety on the road.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-warning-signs-5-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginTop": 34,
                      "marginBottom": 34
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
