                {
                  "id": "h-causes",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Causes Lift Axle Problems?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "causes"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "There are several possible causes behind lift axle issues. Some are simple fixes, while others may require professional trailer service.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-causes-2",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Air System Problems",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Many lift axle systems rely on compressed air to operate correctly. If there's a damaged air line, leaking valve, or faulty airbag, the axle may fail to lift or lower properly.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Common air system issues include:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-causes-5",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 4
                  },
                  "styles": {
                    "base": {
                      "marginBottom": 20
                    }
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "cards-causes-5-1",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-causes-5-1-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Cracked airlines"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Loose fittings"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    },
                    {
                      "id": "cards-causes-5-2",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 6
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
                          "borderColor": "line",
                          "paddingTop": 22,
                          "paddingRight": 22,
                          "paddingBottom": 22,
                          "paddingLeft": 22
                        }
                      },
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "id": "cards-causes-5-2-list",
                          "type": "prose-list",
                          "props": {
                            "ordered": false,
                            "items": [
                              {
                                "text": "Faulty solenoids"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Damaged airbags"
                              },
                              {
                                "text": "Low air pressure"
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-6",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A quick inspection can sometimes reveal visible leaks or worn components, but more complex air system issues often require experienced technicians.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-causes-7",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Electrical Failures",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-8",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Modern lift axle systems often include electrical controls and sensors. Damaged wiring, blown fuses, or malfunctioning switches can interfere with operation. If your lift axle responds inconsistently or not at all, electrical diagnostics may be necessary to identify the problem.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h3-causes-9",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension Wear and Damage",
                    "headingLevel": 3,
                    "align": "left"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-causes-10",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Suspension components naturally wear over time, especially under heavy loads and long hauls. Bushings, shocks, brackets, and other semi-trailer parts can loosen or fail after years of use. Routine inspections help catch wear before it becomes a serious safety issue.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/lift-axle-troubleshooting-for-trailer-owners/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Silhouette of technicians walking toward the service bay doors at dusk"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-preventive",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Preventive Maintenance Matters",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "preventive"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "One of the best ways to avoid lift axle failures is by following a consistent trailer preventive maintenance checklist. Preventive maintenance helps extend the life of your equipment, improve safety, and reduce costly downtime.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>A strong maintenance routine should include:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-preventive-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Checking airbags and air lines"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Inspecting suspension components"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Testing lift axle controls"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Monitoring tire wear patterns"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Lubricating moving parts"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Inspecting electrical connections"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Verifying axle alignment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-preventive-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For fleet owners, preventive maintenance also helps reduce unexpected service interruptions that can affect delivery schedules and customer relationships. At Sun State Trailers, our service department helps customers stay ahead of problems before they become major repairs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-schedule",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Schedule Service With Sun State Trailers",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "schedule"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-schedule-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If your trailer is experiencing lift axle issues, don't wait for a breakdown or roadside inspection to force repairs. The team at <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a> can inspect your suspension system, diagnose lift axle problems, and help you get back on the road with confidence.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/lift-axle-troubleshooting-for-trailer-owners/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State service advisor and shop foreman reviewing a work order at the front counter"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-cost",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Cost of Ignoring Lift Axle Issues",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "cost"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A lift axle problem may seem minor at first, but waiting too long can lead to bigger expenses. Improper weight distribution can place additional strain on tires, brakes, suspension systems, and axles. Over time, this can lead to:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-cost-2",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Premature tire replacement"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Reduced fuel efficiency"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension damage"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "DOT violations"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Increased downtime"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Unsafe driving conditions"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-cost-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "For owner-operators, downtime directly impacts income. Missed deliveries and unexpected repairs create stress not only for drivers, but also for their clients and employees. That's why dependable trailer service matters.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-when-pro",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When to Schedule Professional Trailer Service",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "when-pro"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-pro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Some basic inspections can be handled in-house, but certain lift axle issues require experienced technicians and specialized equipment.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-pro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>You should <a href=\"/contact\">schedule professional trailer service</a> if:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-when-pro-3",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "The axle will not lift or lower"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "You hear constant air leaks"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Suspension components appear damaged"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Tire wear becomes uneven"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Warning lights remain active"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "The trailer feels unstable during operation"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-when-pro-4",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State Trailers, our service teams understand the importance of getting equipment repaired quickly and correctly. We work with customers every day who need reliable solutions without unnecessary delays or confusion.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-keep-moving",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Keep Your Trailer Moving Forward",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "keep-moving"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-keep-moving-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Lift axle problems can quickly turn into larger repair issues if left unchecked. Staying proactive with inspections, maintenance, and professional trailer service helps reduce downtime and keeps your equipment performing the way it should. Contact our team at <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a> to schedule service, inspect your trailer, and keep your equipment road-ready.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
